spans.s:
गुण॑ m. thread, cord, rope, string (adj. —˚ after a num. =
fold or — times, lit. threaded);
 division, species, kind;
 anything
secondary or unessential, e.g. the seasoning of a dish (opp. अन्न),
(g.) the secondary object (cf. गणकर्मन्), the articulation (opp.
स्थान), the secondary gradation (opp. वृद्धि);
 (ph.) the quality,
peculiarity or attribute (opp. द्रव्य or स्वभाव), one of the five
attributes or the three qualities;
 good quality, virtue, excellence;
merit, high degree, pl. the six or four measures of royal policy. Abstr.
गुणता f., ˚त्व n.

गुणमय a. consisting of threads;
 containing the three
qualities;
 virtuous.

गुणवन्त् a. having a thread (virtues);
 possessed of the
five qualities (cf. गुण);
 virtues, excellent, useful, good. Compar.
गुणवत्तर, superl. ˚त्तम.

गुणालय m. the (very) seat of virtues;
 adj. most
virtuous.

गुणिन् a. having a cord (virtues);
 having parts, qualities,
advantages, or merits;
 auspicious, lucky (day);
 object, thing,
substantive.

गुणी w. अस् or भू submit, yield to (gen.);
 pp.
गुणीभूत subject to (gen.), also = गुणभूत.
